// S441 reproducer — item 14: `db=` (and `ratelimit=`) on <page> is SPEC-sanctioned but unimplemented.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/page-db-attr-w-attr-001.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: SPEC §4.15 (SPEC.md:~1097) + §40.8 (SPEC.md:~24205): "The five per-route attributes are
//           `db=`, `auth=`, `csrf=`, `ratelimit=`, `keep-alive`" — db= accepted and scoping the page's `?{}`.
// Actual:   exit 1. `warning [W-ATTR-001]: Attribute `db=` is not recognized on `<page>`. It is currently
//           forwarded to the rendered HTML as-is and has no compile-time effect.` (same for `ratelimit=`), then
//           `error [E-SQL-004]: a `?{}` SQL block has no `db=` declaration in any ancestor `<program>`` —
//           the page's db= is inert. The warning is accurate about the implementation; the implementation
//           is behind the SPEC. Registry root (traced): compiler/src/attribute-registry.js
//           ELEMENT_ATTR_REGISTRY.set("page") omits db + ratelimit; db scopes are read only from
//           `<program db=>` (codegen/index.ts annotateDbScopes) and `<db src=>` (emit-server.ts collectDbScopes).
<program>
<page db="notes.db" ratelimit="100/min">
    function count() { return ?{`SELECT 1 AS n`}.get() }
    <n> = 0
    <button onclick=count()>go</button>
    <p>${@n}</p>
</page>
</program>
